rithm with exponentially improved dependence on precision. Preprint\n806:[11] Lloyd, S., Mohseni, M. & Rebentrost, P. Quantum principal component\n811:[13] Rebentrost, P., Mohseni, M. & Lloyd, S. Quantum support vector machine\n815:[14] Lloyd, S., Garnerone, S. & Zanardi, P. Quantum algorithms for topological\n831:[18] Brandao, F. G. & Svore, K. Quantum speed-ups for semidefinite program-\n844:     & Melko, R.          Quantum Boltzmann machine. Preprint at\n862:     H. J. Quantum speedup for active learning agents. Phys. Rev. X 4, 031002\n884:     tion quantum data.\n923:     for training support vector machines. Neural Netw. 16, 763–770 (2003).\n929:     ing kernels, and quantum support vector machines.         Preprint at\n935:     support vector machine. Phys. Rev. Lett. 114, 140504 (2015). DOI\n947:[53] Lloyd, S., Garnerone, S. & Zanardi, P. Quantum algorithms for topological\n958:     timation of effective temperatures in quantum annealers for sampling\n969:     perimental target for non-stoquastic D-Wave quantum annealing hardware\n970:     able to realize universal quantum Boltzmann machines.\n973:     Quantum metropolis sampling. Nature 471, 87–90 (2011).\n979:     sampling and hitting-time estimation. Quant. Inf. Comp. 17, 0041–0064\n982:     data modeling via quantum Boltzmann training.         Preprint at\n1139:[106] Rønnow, T. F. et al. Defining and detecting quantum speedup. Science\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
